variantes.contenu_markdown:
The first product is glucose (oxygen is released as a by-product). The glucose is then:
- used in respiration to release energy;
- changed to starch for storage in leaves, roots, tubers and seeds;
- changed to sucrose, which is carried in the phloem to growing and storage regions;
- changed to cellulose to build new cell walls;
- changed to fats and oils, stored in seeds such as groundnuts;
- joined with nitrate and other mineral ions from the soil to make amino acids, which form proteins.
